<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#kinyarwanda">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kinyarwanda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kinyarwanda is the Bantu language of Rwanda, spoken by nearly the whole population and closely related to Kirundi of Burundi. In the precolonial kingdom it was shared by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a>, Tutsi and Twa alike, and the royal court cultivated a rich tradition of dynastic poetry and oral history in it. It is one of the official languages of Rwanda.</p></div>
